(ARTICLE 4 SECURITY DEPOSIT) Tj T*
(4.1. Security Deposit. Resident shall pay a security deposit of $300.00. Landlord shall hold the security deposit in a separate non-interest-bearing) Tj T*
(account in a Florida banking institution for the benefit of Resident.) Tj T*
(4.2. Deductions. Landlord may deduct from the security deposit unpaid rent, late charges, the cost of repairing damage beyond normal wear and tear to) Tj T*
(Resident's bedroom and bathroom, Resident's equal share of damage to the shared areas of the Unit under Section 3.4, cleaning charges, and any other) Tj T*
(amount due under this Lease. Landlord shall return the security deposit, or give notice of its intention to impose a claim on it, as required by) Tj T*
(Section 83.49, Florida Statutes.) Tj T*
(4.3. Guarantor. Resident's parent or guardian shall sign a separate Guaranty of this Lease before Resident moves in.) Tj T*
(4.4. Forwarding Address. Resident shall give Landlord a written forwarding address before moving out.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ARTICLE 5 UTILITIES AND SERVICES) Tj T*
(5.1. Included Services. Rent includes water, sewer, trash removal, high-speed internet \(Wi-Fi\), and basic cable television. Electricity is included up) Tj T*
(to a monthly cap of $100.00 per Unit, and any amount over the cap is divided equally among the residents of the Unit.) Tj T*
(5.2. Interruption of Services. Landlord is not liable for any interruption or failure of utilities, internet, or other services caused by a provider,) Tj T*
(a repair, or anything beyond Landlord's reasonable control, and no such interruption entitles Resident to any reduction or abatement of Rent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ARTICLE 6 AMENITIES) Tj T*
(6.1. Community Amenities. Resident may use the swimming pool, fitness center, study rooms, and clubhouse, subject to the Community Rules and posted) Tj T*
(hours.) Tj T*
(6.2. Closure of Amenities. Landlord may close any amenity, in whole or in part, for maintenance, repair, weather, or safety, for as long as Landlord) Tj T*
(reasonably determines. The closure of an amenity does not entitle Resident to any reduction of Rent or any refund of the amenity fee.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ARTICLE 7 MAINTENANCE AND REPAIRS) Tj T*
(7.1. Landlord's Repairs. Landlord shall maintain in good working order and repair the heating, air-conditioning, plumbing, and electrical systems) Tj T*
(serving the Unit and the appliances Landlord furnishes, including the refrigerator, range, dishwasher, microwave, washer, and dryer, except for damage) Tj T*
(caused by Resident, a roommate, or their guests.) Tj T*
(7.2. Maintenance Requests. Resident shall report every repair need by submitting a maintenance request through the online resident portal, except in) Tj T*
(an emergency, which Resident shall report by calling the after-hours emergency line at \(352\) 555-0147. Loss of air-conditioning when the outside) Tj T*
(temperature is above 85 degrees, loss of all water, and an active water leak are emergencies. A maintenance request is a request for service and is) Tj T*
(not by itself a notice under Section 13.1.) Tj T*
(7.3. Time for Repairs. Landlord will make repairs within a reasonable time after Resident's request, considering the availability of parts and) Tj T*
(contractors. Resident is not entitled to any reduction of Rent for inconvenience from a repair or a delay in a repair, except as required by law.) Tj T*
(7.4. Resident's Duties. Resident shall keep the Premises clean and sanitary, shall not block air-conditioning vents, shall report any leak, mold, or) Tj T*
(malfunction promptly, and shall pay for the repair of damage caused by Resident, a roommate, or their guests, including clogged drains and damage to) Tj T*
(appliances from misuse.) Tj T*
(7.5. Permission to Enter. Submitting a maintenance request gives Landlord permission to enter the Unit to make the repair.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Magnolia Row Student Housing Lease | Page 2 of 3) Tj
