(ARTICLE 8 USE AND CONDUCT) Tj T*
(8.1. Use. Resident shall use the Premises only as a private residence for Resident and shall comply with all laws and the Community Rules, which are) Tj T*
(part of this Lease.) Tj T*
(8.2. Guests. A guest may not stay in the Unit more than three \(3\) nights in any thirty \(30\) day period without the written consent of Landlord and of) Tj T*
(every resident of the Unit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ARTICLE 9 MOVE-OUT) Tj T*
(9.1. Move-Out Requirements. At the end of the term Resident shall remove all personal property, clean Resident's bedroom and bathroom, return all keys) Tj T*
(and access cards to the leasing office, and complete a move-out inspection form. Each key or access card not returned is charged at $75.00.) Tj T*
(9.2. Notice Before Vacating. If Resident vacates the Premises before the end of the term, Resident shall give Landlord at least seven \(7\) days') Tj T*
(written notice by certified mail or personal delivery before vacating. If Resident does not give this notice, Resident shall forfeit the security) Tj T*
(deposit as permitted by Section 83.49\(5\), Florida Statutes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ARTICLE 10 DEFAULT) Tj T*
(10.1. Default. If Resident fails to pay any installment of Rent when due, or fails to comply with this Lease, Landlord may end this Lease and recover) Tj T*
(possession of the Premises as provided in Chapter 83, Part II, Florida Statutes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ARTICLE 11 RELETTING) Tj T*
(11.1. Reassignment. Resident may assign this Lease to a replacement resident only with Landlord's written approval and payment of a reassignment fee) Tj T*
(of $250.00.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ARTICLE 12 EARLY TERMINATION) Tj T*
(12.1. Early Termination Option. Resident may end this Lease early by giving Landlord at least sixty \(60\) days' written notice and paying an early) Tj T*
(termination fee of $1,578.00, an amount that does not exceed two \(2\) months' Rent.) Tj T*
(12.2. Servicemembers. Resident may end this Lease early as provided in Section 83.682, Florida Statutes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ARTICLE 13 NOTICES) Tj T*
(13.1. Notices to Landlord. Every notice from Resident to Landlord under this Lease or Florida law must be in writing and delivered by hand to the) Tj T*
(leasing office at 2600 SW Hartwell Lane, Gainesville, Florida 32608, sent by certified mail to that address, or sent by e-mail to) Tj T*
(office@magnoliarow.example.) Tj T*
(13.2. Notices to Resident. Landlord may give notice to Resident by hand delivery, by posting on the door of the Unit, or by e-mail to the address) Tj T*
(Resident gave on the resident portal.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ARTICLE 14 SIGNATURES) Tj T*
(RESIDENT: Sam Patel Date: July 20, 2026) Tj T*
(LANDLORD: Hartwell Residential Management, LLC, as agent for MR Gainesville Owner, LLC By: Dana Whitfield, Community Manager Date: July 22, 2026) Tj T*
() Tj T*
